### Documentation Rules

> Rule of thumb: stable material that a second task will reuse goes to `.docs/`; anything that only serves one work episode goes to `.project/`.

- **`.docs/` shared material**: environment and access details, feature lists, API/data-reporting specs, resource and component inventories, acceptance and test reports — relatively stable material reused across tasks
- **`.project/` workspace**: requirement discussions, design notes, demo and verification runs, debugging, Q&A records, development plans and retrospectives
- `.docs/` groups material into category directories with a two-digit numeric prefix for ordering: `01-environments/` (fixed), `02-feature-list/`, `03-data-reporting/`; `00-` can be reserved for overview or glossary material
- **Do not use `YYYYMMDD-` date directories inside `.docs/`**; append new categories at the end of the numbering — never renumber or reuse an old number
- `.docs/README.md` is the shared-material index: register every new, moved, or split category there
- Keep each shared document and its attachments in exactly one place; topic directories under `.project/` link to `.docs/` with relative paths instead of copying files
- When several versions of a document exist, keep only the latest and record the version in the filename or the body — not in a dated directory
- **One topic, one directory** under `.project/`: tasks on the same topic share a single `<topic>/` directory. For complex work, use numbered subdirectories such as `01-discussion` inside that directory instead of creating another topic directory
- {{OTHER_DOCUMENTATION_REQUIREMENTS}}

### Environment Rules

- Environment and access details are shared material: keep them in `.docs/01-environments/`, one file per environment named `test.md` / `uat.md` / `prd.md`
- Only create files for environments that actually exist: do not invent files or placeholder content for missing environments — note them in the "Environment Index" instead
- Edit the environment file in place when details change; do not keep historical versions. Mask sensitive fields per team policy

### Task Tracking

> One register, one detail location: the root `TODO.md` is the index and `.project/` holds the details.

- For a new task, create `.project/YYYYMMDD-<topic>/` and name the body after the topic
- Merge follow-up work on the same topic into the existing topic directory (use numbered subdirectories such as `01-discussion` for steps); do not create a second topic directory
- Add one line under "In Progress" in the root `TODO.md`: `### <item>, see [<directory>](.project/<directory>)`
- When done, move the item from "In Progress" to "Completed / Archived" with a `### ✅` prefix
- Promote lasting conclusions into `.docs/`; do not pile process detail into the root `TODO.md` or topic directories

